---
import EditorialShell from '../../components/EditorialShell.astro';

const currentUrl = new URL(Astro.url.pathname, Astro.site ?? 'https://shivammahajan.com').href;
const structuredData = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@graph': [
    {
      '@type': 'BlogPosting',
      '@id': `${currentUrl}#article`,
      isPartOf: { '@id': 'https://shivammahajan.com/#website' },
      headline: "How the SM'S DEX roster works",
      description: "Learn how a GitHub issue becomes an automated, verified, and reviewed developer roster entry in SM'S DEX, Shivam Mahajan's Pokédex-themed portfolio.",
      author: { '@id': 'https://shivammahajan.com/#shivam-mahajan' },
      publisher: { '@id': 'https://shivammahajan.com/#shivam-mahajan' },
      url: currentUrl,
      datePublished: '2026-10-05T00:00:00Z',
      dateModified: '2026-10-05T00:00:00Z'
    },
    {
      '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
      '@id': `${currentUrl}#breadcrumb`,
      itemListElement: [
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://shivammahajan.com/' },
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Blog', item: 'https://shivammahajan.com/blog/' },
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: "How the SM'S DEX roster works", item: currentUrl }
      ]
    }
  ]
};
---
<EditorialShell title="How the SM'S DEX Public Roster Works" description="Learn how a GitHub issue becomes an automated, verified, and reviewed developer roster entry in SM'S DEX, Shivam Mahajan's Pokédex-themed portfolio." eyebrow="Build notes / SM'S DEX" heading="How the SM'S DEX roster works" intro="Visitors submit a character through the site's form. A GitHub issue starts validation, then a pull request gives Shivam a review step before publication." structuredData={structuredData}>
  <a slot="actions" href="/projects/sm-dex/">Explore SM'S DEX</a><a slot="actions" href="https://github.com/smresponsibilities/smresponsibilities.github.io">View repository ↗</a>
  <section><h2>From form to issue</h2><p>The Add Pokémon form collects a GitHub username, species, types, status, and short dex entry. Submitting opens a prefilled issue in the site's GitHub repository. The issue is the public record of what a visitor entered. This ensures transparency and gives every submission a visible paper trail.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Validation and review</h2><p>A GitHub Actions workflow runs when a qualifying issue opens, changes, or receives a label. It parses the issue, runs the submission validator, writes a roster entry, and opens or updates a pull request. Validation errors are posted back to the issue directly via the bot. Shivam securely reviews the generated JSON artifacts before merging the pull request.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Why use a pull request</h2><p>A public form should not publish arbitrary user-generated text instantly. The pull request review process keeps the roster intentional while leaving a visible path from submission to entry. The roster data lives natively in the repository, so the site can securely build from a checked-in copy rather than a vulnerable live database.</p><p>Try the form on the <a href="/">homepage</a>, or read the broader <a href="/projects/sm-dex/">project overview</a>.</p></section>
</EditorialShell>
